@@ -53,6 +53,10 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **Rename refuses occupied names.** Member and class renames preserve distinct declarations, PHP case rules and private inheritance boundaries. Case-only changes and unrelated owners remain available. Parent trait members also follow their effective visibility and class declaration precedence, while inaccessible accesses still report their owning class. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
+
+- **Fresh suggestions after edits.** Background class resolution cannot restore outdated members after an unsaved dependency changes. Nested resolutions and generic specializations retain the same invalidation boundary. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
+
 - **References respect unknown receivers.** Finding usages or renaming a member on an untyped receiver no longer selects same-named members from unrelated classes. Macro registration searches also exclude unrelated or unknown call chains. Known typed and framework receivers keep their scoped results. Contributed by @longdo
 
 - **Nested Composer projects keep independent completion and PHP settings.** Opening a containing Composer workspace also discovers its child projects. Installed libraries retain the consuming application's configuration, and saved manifest changes preserve current unsaved buffers. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
